WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.734
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.767
A lot has happened since you've
been on the show last.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.300
-Yes.
-Yeah, now you just became

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.734
a two-time Tony winner.
Congratulations.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:11.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Two times!

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.234
"A Strange Loop."

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.801
"A Strange Loop" is one of
the greatest musicals

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:17.534
I've ever seen.

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:19.434
Make sure you get your tickets.
-Go see "A Strange Loop."

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:20.701
-And go see it, yeah.

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.901
-How did you get involved with
"A Strange Loop"?

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:26.300
-The producer, Barbara Whitman,
called me up.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.767
And she said she was looking for
celebrity producers.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:34.067
And the story is about -- you
know, it follows a queer man's

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:38.167
story as he tries to sort of
figure out his way as a writer,

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.100
a musical theater writer
in show business.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.334
And I had seen it off Broadway.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:45.234
And never in a million years --
I thought it was brilliant.

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.000
Never in a million years did
I ever think it would make it

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.067
to Broadway because Broadway
didn't have things like that,

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:54.567
so, you know, it's such a gift
and a blessing to see

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:58.667
that kind of change and to see
my own personal story...

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.968
-That story be told.
-...reflected -- yes, reflected

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.067
back at me
in a Broadway musical.

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.267
It's stunning.
-It's good. It's stunning.

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.033
But it's also funny too.
-Yes.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:10.100
-We've had them on the show.
The cast was just amazing.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.133
And when you see everyone get
together, you go, "Oh, my God.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.868
Of course, this is the best."
And it won Best Musical.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.567
-It won Best Musical!
-Congratulations!

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.033
-Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:19.868
-Go see it! Go see it.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:24.767
We had our pal -- Jane Fonda was
on the show the other day.

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.100
-Oh.
-And she showed us a picture of

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.300
this movie
that she's working on.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.634
-Uh-huh.
-And it's her, Rita Moreno,

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.400
it is Lily Tomlin,
it is Sally Field.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.200
-It is Sally Field, yes.
-And Billy Porter and Tom Brady.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.834
-Yes.
-That's the ca--

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.167
-Yes, it is.
-That is the cast.

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:41.133
-[ Laughs ]
-What can you tell us?

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.567
-There are some other people
too.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:46.300
Yes, it's called
"80 for Brady," and it follows

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:51.968
the 2016 Super Bowl, I think,
where he came back.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:53.801
You know, that's not
my ministry.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:58.067
[ Laughter ]
But I heard

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.901
that they came back and won.

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:04.067
And so, four broads
who are Tom Brady fans

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.334
win tickets to the Super Bowl

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.567
and they go to meet Tom Brady
at the Super Bowl.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:10.434
And I play the
choreographer/director

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:12.901
of the halftime show.

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:14.701
I mean, who else?

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.434
-Wait, but at the halftime show,

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:21.634
are you saying is there a Jane
Fonda -- is there a -- not?

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:24.300
-There a little bit of a moment.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.534
There's a little bit of
a choreographic moment.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:29.501
If you blink, you miss it,
but it's fun.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:30.934
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.033
-I want to ask you about this

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.200
because this is
kind of exciting.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.601
I like to be kind of
a matchmaker here on the show.

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:38.133
I heard that --
-Oh.

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:39.868
-You and J.Lo are --

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:42.300
You're on a mission to become
best friends with J.Lo.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.634
[ Laughter ]
And I want to be able to --

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.834
I want to help this,
push this forward.

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.868
You want to be besties with
J.Lo. We all do.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.901
-We can push it forward.
I -- She called me.

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.501
She reached out to me

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:56.968
to introduce her
for her IHeartRadio...

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:58.133
-Oh, yeah. She got honored.
-They were giving her

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.701
a big award.
They were honoring her.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:01.234
-I actually saw this.
You did a great job.

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:03.767
-And so, you know, I did that

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.968
for her because,
I mean, she's J.Lo.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.200
I mean, come on.
-Yeah.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.234
-J.Lo calls, you answer.
-Always.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.601
-And so, I called and we met
and we hung out.

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:15.300
And then she invited me
to dinner afterwards.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.934
And Ben was there.
[ Cheers ]

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:20.067
And I was like,
"Oh, shoot, can we be friends?"

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.734
And they said,
"Yes, we can be friends."

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:26.267
-Any projects coming up
with Jennifer?

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.534
-Not yet, but I'm trying.
-Alright, here we go.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:29.968
Jennifer --
-I'm trying, girl!

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.901
You got that script, honey.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:35.901
Read her after your honeymoon.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:38.067
-After the honeymoon.

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:40.200
You know, last time you were
on the show, I believe,

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.133
we debuted the cover of
your memoir.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:44.567
-Oh, yes.
-And now it is out.

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:46.534
-It is out.
-People can --

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:51.734
People can read it.
Your story's out.

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:53.300
It has so many stories in here.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.067
-Yes, there are. There's a lot.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.434
-I was going to ask you, how do
you choose what gets in the book

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:00.167
and what doesn't get
into the book?

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:02.400
-Well, I'm an overachiever.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:06.133
-You are.
-And you know --

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.601
-You have that in common
with J.Lo.

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:09.701
-Yes, that's why we should be
friends.

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:13.601
-Exactly.
-And my editor -- you know,

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:16.067
I was supposed to give
like 75,000 words.

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:17.467
-Yeah.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:20.968
-You know, true to form, I
turned in about 137,000 words.

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:22.434
-That's exactly right.

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:24.334
-And so, they were like, "We're
going to have to cut this down."

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:28.000
So, legal came in and stepped in
and that's how...

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.234
-They said --
-...we cut it down.

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:30.634
Some of the legal stuff,
they were like,

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:33.334
"Okay, you can't say that."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.868
"You can't say that.
You might get sued."

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:37.100
I'm like,
"Well, it's the truth."

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.667
They're like,
"Yes, it's your truth."

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.400
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.434
But there's some unbelievable
stories in here.

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:45.901
-Thank you.

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:48.000
-It must feel good right now.
-I'm really proud of it. I am.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.400
Go buy it!
-Yeah, go check it out.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.334
-So we can get on "The New York
Times" bestseller list!

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.634
[ Applause ]

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.000
I'm very proud of the work.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.100
-And now you've directed
your very first feature film.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.934
-Yes!
-"Anything's Possible."

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:03.133
-Yes!
-On Prime Video right now.

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.234
"Anything's Possible."
Congratulations.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:06.934
-Thank you.
-Busy, busy, busy.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.701
-Thank you.
-How do we set this up?

00:05:08.701 --> 00:05:10.200
How would you set this film up
for everyone?

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:17.367
-Okay. So, "Anything's Possible"
is a rom-com, coming-of-age tale

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.701
in the spirit of
old John Hughes movies.

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:25.968
But the cast is populated with
what the world looks like today.

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:29.133
Our lead, our heroine is
a Black trans girl

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:30.567
who's a senior in high school.

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:32.567
She gets a boyfriend.
She gets into college.

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:36.300
It's about trans joy.
It's about celebration.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's about celebrating the joy.

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:42.868
And it's pretty magical.
-Yeah, it is.

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:44.934
Not only did you --
You're getting great reviews.

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.100
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.634
-But also, the soundtrack
-Has all original music.

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:51.234
-Yes.
-And a lot of it -- you --

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:55.868
-We did. I executive produced
the album with Justin Tranter

00:05:55.868 --> 00:06:00.067
on my label, Republic Records,
where I'm actually having

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:03.367
my own music come out very soon,
you know, later in the fall.

00:06:03.367 --> 00:06:04.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Ooh!

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:07.133
-I call it adult pop,
so get ready.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.701
-Adult pop?
-I'm coming! I'm coming!

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.701
-In the fall!
-And so, it's coming out.

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:12.834
But this is sort of
a precursor to that.

00:06:12.834 --> 00:06:14.734
I have five brand-new songs that

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:17.067
I wrote with Justin Tranter
and his camp.

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:18.968
And we curated the album.

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:23.067
It's about 90%, I would say,
queer artists.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:25.334
-Yeah. Good for you.
-And it's great.

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:27.267
So, go listen to the album.
I'm trying to bring back

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:30.000
the days when the album was
associated with the movie.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.701
Remember? Y'all remember
"Waiting to Exhale"?

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:34.934
And, you know,
"The Preacher's Wife"

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:37.467
and "The Bodyguard" and stuff?
It was soundtrack!

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:40.133
Honey, the soundtrack
of your life.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:44.300
-I don't want to make any
predictions or say anything,

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:48.701
but already you've won --
you won the Emmy, the Grammy.

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:49.734
-Yes.
-And the Tony.

00:06:49.734 --> 00:06:51.133
-Yes.
-The two Tonys.

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:54.501
-Yes, two-time Tonys.
-So this -- I'm just saying.

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:57.067
You directed a great film.
You did a great soundtrack.

00:06:57.067 --> 00:06:58.634
You sing on this.

00:06:58.634 --> 00:07:00.901
I'm just saying, I'm ready for
an EGOT with two T's.

00:07:00.901 --> 00:07:03.634
-Listen.
-An EGOTT. An EGOTT.

00:07:03.634 --> 00:07:06.634
-From your lips --
-With two T's.

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:09.767
-From your lips to the ears
with two T's, honey.

00:07:09.767 --> 00:07:11.033
-EGOTT.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:12.534
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:14.834
This is "Anything's Possible,"
directed by Billy Porter.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:17.000
Take a look.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.334
-We could live our own life
right now

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:24.667
or do what people expect of us

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:32.434
and spend the rest of our life
wondering what if.

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:41.701
Yes.

00:07:46.367 --> 00:07:49.834
[ Elevator bell dings ]
♪♪

00:07:49.834 --> 00:07:53.167
-I mean, I love that.
I love movies like that.

00:07:53.167 --> 00:07:55.000
I love it.
-Joy. It's about joy, y'all.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.300
-I love joy.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:58.667
Speaking of joy --
-Yes.

00:07:58.667 --> 00:08:00.901
-The cast -- I've read
some articles.

00:08:00.901 --> 00:08:03.334
The cast have said that you're
so fun to work with on set.

00:08:03.334 --> 00:08:06.200
And they said that in almost
every situation, you can make

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.501
any situation
into some musical moment.

00:08:08.501 --> 00:08:10.934
And it reminds you of a song
or you'll start singing.

00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:12.567
And you just made it
so loose and fun.

00:08:12.567 --> 00:08:14.801
So, I thought we --
-Oh, Lord.

00:08:14.801 --> 00:08:18.434
-We always have a spare mike...
-Oh, Lord!

00:08:18.434 --> 00:08:21.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-...just in case.

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:24.801
Is there -- Is there a song --
What are you thinking?

00:08:24.801 --> 00:08:25.968
What are you feeling?

00:08:25.968 --> 00:08:27.834
What would you like to express
and tell --

00:08:27.834 --> 00:08:29.634
-Well, it's funny
you should ask.

00:08:29.634 --> 00:08:32.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.501 --> 00:08:38.200
♪ I love it so much here
and I am telling you ♪

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:40.701 --> 00:08:45.400
♪ I'm not going away ♪

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.634
♪ I'm staying ♪

00:08:47.701 --> 00:08:50.334
♪ I'm staying ♪

00:08:50.334 --> 00:08:53.901
♪ And you and you and you ♪

00:08:53.901 --> 00:08:56.834
♪ You're gonna love meeee ♪

00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:59.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:59.133 --> 00:09:03.868
♪ Hey! ♪

00:09:04.767 --> 00:09:14.501
♪ You're gonna loooooooooove ♪

00:09:14.501 --> 00:09:15.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:15.868 --> 00:09:20.467
♪ Meeeeeeeeeeeeee ♪

00:09:20.467 --> 00:09:24.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:24.968 --> 00:09:27.334
-Are you kidding me?!

00:09:27.334 --> 00:09:29.200
Oh, my goodness!

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:30.968
Look at that! Look at that!

00:09:30.968 --> 00:09:32.067
Look at that, buddy!

00:09:32.067 --> 00:09:34.534
Come on. Look at that!
Standing ovation.

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:36.067
Billy Porter.
-Thank you.

00:09:36.067 --> 00:09:37.701
-We all need to love him.

00:09:37.701 --> 00:09:39.834
"Anything's Possible."
That's amazing.

00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:42.601
Streaming now, "Anything's
Possible," on Prime Video.

00:09:42.601 --> 00:09:44.467
More "Tonight Show"
after the break, everybody.

